00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.650
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So
are VPCs something

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.055
that could help on
what you were talking?

00:18:18.055 --> 00:18:20.180
What is actually a
VPC and how could it

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:22.860
help make our solution safer?

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:26.850
INES ENVID: So the VPC, it's
really-- you can think of it,

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.850
again, I used the
term before, but you

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:33.720
can think of it as the
sandbox where you are actually

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.250
running your application.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:40.280
So if you, as a user, have
your production environment,

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.020
your production
environment is going

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.630
to run in a private space.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:48.100
You don't want to expose
it to the internet.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:51.720
So those applications in
your production environment

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:54.560
are going to be talking
across each other.

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.610
You have rules that are going
to define how they actually

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:02.160
communicate and you have
your perimeter defined

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.780
for those applications.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.400
Any communication
external, then,

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.580
is going to be controlled,
again, with firewall rules.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:11.080
So it gives you private
space, like in an in-network,

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.264
and it will be a
private IP space where

00:19:13.264 --> 00:19:14.680
you are mapping
your applications,

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:18.040
you are running your services
while you are securing

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.790
against the outside world.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:25.460
And there are great ways
of leverage that sandbox

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:28.120
and that private IP applications
when you're actually

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.370
working in Google environment.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.370
Some of them are,
for instance, access

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:39.780
to Google services like Storage
