00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.360
there is all the data
ingestion and data processing

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:46.180
capabilities.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:48.770
You can actually access
those from your VPC,

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:52.010
which is, again, your private
environment, privately as well.

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.610
So that when you're
communicating your workloads

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:58.510
to get access to all the
APIs and service capabilities

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:04.170
that Google offer, think as well
about machine learning APIs.

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:09.270
So you do that in a secure
way via private communication.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.780
So it's really a way
of building, truly,

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:17.510
your private cloud while
it is all virtualized,

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:20.720
because it gives you
the illusion that you

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.470
are running your
own infrastructure,

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.460
you're running
your own services.

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:28.120
But what it does is, of course,
gives you all the flexibility

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.620
