00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:48.258
it is definitely
top-class network.

00:31:48.258 --> 00:31:53.040
And leveraging on that,
then are all the policies

00:31:53.040 --> 00:31:55.410
that we talk about,
so then it helps

00:31:55.410 --> 00:31:59.750
you to have the perception
that you are just

00:31:59.750 --> 00:32:02.450
unique in that infrastructure
and that you aren't just

00:32:02.450 --> 00:32:05.840
operating your own
environment, well, you

00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:08.460
are having all these
amazing capabilities

00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:09.796
and access to storage.

00:32:09.796 --> 00:32:14.290
And if you need to spin
100 more instances,

00:32:14.290 --> 00:32:16.790
you don't need to worry
about buying more servers,

00:32:16.790 --> 00:32:20.280
and then all the sudden, you
get the same great capabilities

00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:22.460
that you had in the first
instance that you built.

00:32:22.460 --> 00:32:28.385
So I think this is one of the
biggest assets of Google Cloud.

00:32:28.385 --> 00:32:29.260
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yes.

00:32:29.260 --> 00:32:30.630
What you were saying
